WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:05.502
(dubstep music)

00:00:11.079 --> 00:00:13.406
- [Voiceover] Jodhpur,
India is a sea of blue

00:00:13.406 --> 00:00:17.022
in the middle of a hot, dry desert.

00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:19.105
Welcome to the Blue City.

00:00:23.654 --> 00:00:25.390
Jodhpur is the second largest city

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.902
in India's Rajasthan province.

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:29.718
Surrounded by a wall with bastions,

00:00:29.718 --> 00:00:33.190
the striking blue buildings
in Jodhpur contrast sharply

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.662
and beautifully with the
neighboring Thar Desert.

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:40.567
It's the older quarters, built in 1459,

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:43.283
where many of the blue
buildings are found.

00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:46.554
Some say the color is associated
closely with the Brahmans,

00:00:46.554 --> 00:00:48.923
India's priestly caste,
and the blue houses

00:00:48.923 --> 00:00:53.170
of the old city belong to
families of that caste.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:56.258
There's also an argument that
termites are the real reason.

00:00:56.258 --> 00:00:58.457
Builders added copper
sulfate to the whitewash

00:00:58.457 --> 00:00:59.978
to thwart the pests,

00:00:59.978 --> 00:01:03.410
which resulted in the eye-soothing blue.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.577
However, locals say the blue
is a natural indigo dye.

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:11.115
A final explanation might
be the city's nickname.

00:01:11.115 --> 00:01:13.589
It's known as the Sun City,

00:01:13.589 --> 00:01:16.839
and the blue helps keep the homes cool.

00:01:17.956 --> 00:01:21.437
Either way, Jodhpur looks
like a real life fairytale.

00:01:21.437 --> 00:01:25.020
(calming electronic music)

